## Role execution guidance
- exploit: take the best diagnostic survivors and push them through aligned
  (max_points 350..500). Confirm or kill with the pre-registered gate.
- falsifier: do NOT chase the leaderboard. Design the ablation that would
  DISPROVE the most load-bearing mechanism claim (e.g. run the candidate
  WITHOUT the covariate as a control variant, same window). Publish
  finding_type=challenge via share_finding if the control matches the
  treatment.
- bridge: combine two non-redundant covariate families on one symbol (e.g.
  CCL positioning x rsi_state) and ablate each component explicitly.
- anti_mainline: your candidates are FORBIDDEN from using the dominant
  families (see anti_mainline contract above if present, else the families
  already on the frontier). Cover the neglected families: oi, ccl,
  basis_momentum, volume-related, calendar_cyclical.

## End-of-generation checklist
1. Every candidate passed to the evaluator inline via --candidate <(echo '...')
   or written under the run_dir peer workspace. Do NOT use scripts/praxist_ws/
   (blocked by delete guard).
2. Every evaluation written to the canonical tree
   {{ results_dir | default("<run_dir>/results") }}/gen_{{ gen_id | default(0) }}/{{ peer_id | default("peer") }}/<variant_id>/<stage>/
3. Every hypothesis/insight/challenge published via share_finding with
   metrics and links. Result findings flow from evaluation summaries.
4. Done means: evidence landed in the canonical tree, not in your workspace.
